{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 as a passive FTP upload destination using the scanner account specified in access.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The scanner credentials were read from the staged handover, the account and dedicated FTP root were created on node1, and passive FTP sessions from node2 authenticated successfully and negotiated data ports in the configured passive range.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f6292451a844271","cmd-e3f848579af64633","cmd-c96f9dabdaa44899","cmd-b13ff22bd1bc4c36"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the scanner to upload and retrieve files, including the supplied sample scan.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 uploaded sample-scan.txt through PASV, retrieved it through a separate PASV session, and verified a byte-for-byte match and the staged sample's SHA-256 hash. A complete upload/retrieval round trip also succeeded after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b13ff22bd1bc4c36","cmd-4f56b0c5711a4a7e","cmd-0906b5df2fb74eee"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Confine the scanner account to its dedicated dropbox and prevent access to host files outside it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account is chrooted under a root-owned FTP root containing a scanner-owned dropbox. Attempted traversal to host /etc/passwd returned no content, a root-level upload was rejected with FTP 553, and final inspection confirmed that the forbidden file was absent and only the dropbox was scanner-writable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc956479076d4c97","cmd-53bdf044a7a24a90","cmd-cae4513af5704d04"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Disable anonymous FTP access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An anonymous authentication attempt was directly rejected with FTP 530. The final configuration also explicitly retained anonymous_enable=NO.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e7fd18f1554840af","cmd-cae4513af5704d04"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed server was Xenial's vsftpd 3.0.3-3ubuntu2 package. Both nodes remained Ubuntu 16.04.7 with kernel 4.4.0-210-generic after execution and restart, matching their pre-execution platform observations.","evidence_ids":["cmd-062dc23440b149df","cmd-6f7ea2b024994caa","cmd-1ac9a38dfb3247c1","cmd-0906b5df2fb74eee","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.99,"summary":"No unnecessary state-changing mutations were identified. Package installation, account/directory creation, configuration, service enablement, and seeded-file placement were causally related to the requested FTP destination. Both reboots served the mandatory provider restart protocol. Evidence probes used bounded temporary files and cleaned them; the failed first anonymous-access assertion only reflected an overly specific expected error string and did not leave retained state. Final snapshots show healthy package state, no failed services, and only normal reboot-created systemd temporary directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6f7ea2b024994caa","cmd-e3f848579af64633","cmd-c96f9dabdaa44899","cmd-cb05d47e9ec34921","cmd-014b2ef121ab4053","cmd-659c973ebd0f49d2","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct behavior and final-state evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/data behavior. Node1 recovered its enabled listener and file hashes and served a passive retrieval; node2 retained its source data and completed a post-restart passive round trip.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-sockets observation for node1 is empty despite direct commands shortly beforehand showing an active port-21 listener and successful post-restart FTP transfers. Because the lifecycle socket collector was also empty before execution and direct service evidence is coherent, this is treated as a collector limitation, but it modestly lowers confidence.","General confinement is supported by chroot configuration, ownership, a traversal attempt against /etc/passwd, and denial of a root-level write; the evidence does not attempt retrieval of numerous distinct host paths."]}
